#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:166
#: c4983e3f80b248838a72960301717a1a
msgid "You’re not finished fiddling with this yet but what you will find is that these settings make the yaw control much stronger then on previous versions of the software and also help reduce the very small oscillation it used to have."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:172
#: c0813e757065487aa10290e7d8d1a55b
msgid "Acro Mode Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:174
#: b5415dbe64df433897f5885050d0c11b
msgid "The AXIS_ENABLE parameter should be set to 1 otherwise Acro mode will be unflyable. AXIS_ENABLE basically turns on a 3-D \"heading lock\" gyro mode that works very well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:178
#: 04f6718d1d854f83b22be38c5f55cea6
msgid "There are a few other parameters you should know about:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:180
#: fbfeb863282c434b87ff8511fe0118a2
msgid "ACRO_BAL_PITCH and ACRO_BAL_ROLL: These create a \"virtual dihedral\" which attempts to return the heli to level. This is what Leonard calls \"Acro with training wheels\". 200 makes it feel almost like stabilize. If you fly with it on 50 it feels nice. 0 would obviously turn it off completely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:186
#: 8b98ad9fb4f24903800fa5388c7e89d2
msgid "ACRO_TRAINER: This is in addition to ACRO_BAL_ROLL and prevents the heli from rolling past 45°. You can push it a bit beyond but it won't go too far. If you don’t want it, just turn it off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:190
#: c9298f64314d4896bd3551836fc6f12d
msgid "If you want to speed up the angular rate, you will want to play with ACRO_P which defaults to 4.5 which gives you a rate of 202°/s. Set at 6 will give about 270°/s and 8 will give about 360°/s. The gyros have a full scale of 2,000°/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:196
#: b23a90fa402445618342770a2e3e10cb
msgid "Stabilization Mode Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:198
#: bade911b0af64fda8c1df33262e65004
msgid "One of the things you should look at is your STAB_PIT_P and STAB_RLL_P numbers? These were probably quite low in version 2.7.3, probably less than 1, and they should now be 3.5 to 4.5. This is a really big factor in getting the servo movement you are expecting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:204
#: 2f086238eacf4785bdbd39add5f9ea5e
msgid "Throttle Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:206
#: d747493321c64f5a8ad1875e133afa0b
msgid "THR_MID convert's the pilot's throttle input (0~1000) to the motor output (130~1000). It has two different scales so that the pilot's 0~500 input maps to the 130~THR_MID value...then another scale so pilot's 501~1000 input is mapped to the THR_MID~1000 output for the motor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:211
#: 5e9e85acade14974b2f855b0c6556fd9
msgid "Essentially THR_MID should be the throttle setting for hover."
msgstr ""

