#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:246
#: f55ae40af75e414d93179f67efa06d6c
msgid "Aerobatics in Acro Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:248
#: e4e4b86c863948deb02c038acee19a24
msgid "Acro Mode in APM:Copter now supports full acrobatic flight!  The function is similar to any other acrobatic FBL controller available on the market.  The performance might not be suitable for helicopter competition, but it certainly adequate for sport flying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:253
#: 101903db3ddb414c99e6d6df73df2cd0
msgid "Many maneuvers have been fully tested, loops, rolls, inverted flight, etc.  Caution should be exercised if aggressive 3D type maneuvers are attempted, such as tic-tocs, etc.  While the control algorithms are fine, it's unproven if the system is able to maintain its orientation relative the ground.  In other FBL controllers, if this were to happen, the controller would simply turn off the self-leveling function but the acrobatic flight can continue as normal.  But with APM:Copter, this could lead to loss of control even in Acro mode. We will attempt to remedy this situation in the future so that all maneuvers can be performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:264
#: ff3f64c5d55942c6b43a36b0075b7b6d
msgid "ACRO_BAL_PITCH = 50"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:266
#: 3076a9415607496d8cd7197759d69970
msgid "ACRO_BAL_ROLL = 50"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:268
#: 26b3073dfd9d4b038d6fcb1e8b24b7f0
msgid "ACRO_P = 4.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:270
#: 462de033185948ceaafdef15fcc694c5
msgid "ACRO_TRAINER = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:273
#: ad2bbf466aa1456ba5341eb919ef02a0
msgid "AXIS_ENABLE = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:275
#: 6e14c7a747a04febb18a99c74706f6d5
msgid "ACRO_P is basically the angular rate. 4.5 gives you 202.5°/s. 9 would give you 405. But nobody has pushed that high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:278
#: b91533f1135f4e1bb74df9bf987b09ab
msgid "ACRO_BAL_ROLL is like a faked \"dihedral\" effect. It makes the copter return to level gently at center stick. 50 is fairly low, 200 makes it feel almost like Stabilize."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:282
#: 71512e714a1d4f64a065ad3ad28fb74e
msgid "ACRO_TRAINER is an addition thing that makes the heli not want to roll past 45°."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:285
#: f389270cceda410d88ccb2c52ceece34
msgid "AXIS_ENABLE turns the whole angle-lock thing on. Sort of like Futaba AVCS in all 3 axes. Without it, it's pure rate control and your experience will be pretty bad."
msgstr ""
